## `tools/` and `skills/`

`tools/` and `skills/` are Edittude's own code and are covered by the root `LICENSE` (MIT for that code, Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Torres). HKU Data Intelligence Lab's [VideoAgent](https://github.com/HKUDS/VideoAgent) is inspiration only.

`tools/README.md` says the implementation imports no Edittude or HKU modules. `skills/README.md` and `AGENTS.md` describe the pack as inspired by HKU VideoAgent. `skills/` includes 10 Edittude-only skills: `aspect-reframe`, `assembly`, `color-grade`, `editorial-taste`, `footage-inventory`, `iterate-recut`, `mix`, `review-qc`, `titles`, and `zero-shot-cut`. `skills/manifest.json` records [HKUDS/VideoAgent](https://github.com/HKUDS/VideoAgent) at commit `f207987e3cffb554aaa6ffdbe733efb30f4b51ed` as the source of the 33 `video-*` role mappings.

A git-blob comparison of the 71 files under `tools/` and `skills/` against that commit matched only `tools/LICENSE` and `skills/LICENSE`. Those files were byte-identical to VideoAgent `LICENSE` (sha256 `68c9fc511bb10d1488522aa139d1e91289b76ab998fc8ca815e93a85c4ea4850`), Copyright (c) 2025 Data Intelligence Lab@HKU. They covered no HKU code and are removed. Checked: <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HKUDS/VideoAgent/f207987e3cffb554aaa6ffdbe733efb30f4b51ed/LICENSE>.

